    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, I'm glad you could make it in today. What brings you in to see me?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S014",
      "patient_response": "Well, hello. Thank you for seeing me. I suppose I'm here because my daughter suggested it. She says I'm just... well, she says I'm always up and moving. And I suppose she's right. Even on a quiet day, I'm bouncing from the garden club list to my knitting bag to travel papers before I've really finished any one thing. Oh, speaking of travel papers, my husband and I went to Florida last winter, and you wouldn't believe the humidity! My hair was just an absolute disaster the entire time. We stayed at this lovely little place right on the beach, though. They had these wonderful little complimentary soaps in the bathroom, shaped like seashells. I brought a whole bag of them home for the guest bath. Anyway, what was I saying? Oh, right, my daughter thinks I just can't seem to sit still and finish a project.",
