    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Have you been this way for as long as you can remember since childhood, or is this something that started more recently?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Oh my, no, this isn't a new thing at all. It's been my whole life, really. Even back in grade school, my teachers used to tell my mother that I was a bright girl, but just terribly scattered. I was always losing my papers. \n\nWhich reminds me, I just lost my favorite recipe card for peach cobbler the other day! I was going to make it for the church bake sale. We have a bake sale every spring to raise money for the choir robes, and let me tell you, those robes are getting so worn out. The hems on the tenor section are just fraying to bits, and I told Pastor Dave we really need to look into a different dry cleaner because the chemicals they use are just too harsh on the fabric. \n\nBut oh, where was I? Right, grade school. Yes, my teachers said I was always talking out of turn, just chatting away, and wiggling around in my seat before I ever finished my work. I just couldn't seem to sit still even back then.",
