    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Do you ever have times where you can get by on very little sleep, like just a few hours, and still feel completely energized?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Oh, goodness, no. If I only get a few hours of sleep, I am just dragging the next day. I really need my solid seven or eight hours. \n\nWe actually just bought a new mattress last year because my back was starting to bother me on the old one. We went down to that big furniture place on Route 4... oh, what's it called? Mattress King? Something like that. Anyway, the salesman there was wearing the loudest plaid suit I have ever seen in my life. It was bright yellow and green! I whispered to my husband, \"He looks like a walking lemon-lime soda.\" My husband just shushed me—he hates when I make comments like that in public—but I couldn't help it! \n\nWe ended up buying a memory foam one, which is lovely, but it is just so heavy to lift when you're putting the fitted sheet on. I always have to buy the deep-pocket sheets now because the regular ones just pop right off the corners in the middle of the night, and there is nothing worse than waking up sleeping on a bare mattress pad. I found a lovely set on sale at the department store, a very soft lavender color... \n\nBut... oh, wait, what were you asking me? About sleep? Right, yes, I definitely need my sleep. I've never been one of those people who can just run on fumes and feel energized, that's for sure.",
