    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "{\"intent\": \"Assess whether the attention and restlessness symptoms cause significant functional impairment in daily life\", \"question\": \"Do these difficulties with staying focused and sitting still cause significant problems or interference in your",
      "targeted_symptom": "functional_impairment",
      "patient_response": "Well, I suppose they do cause some problems, yes. It's really started causing a strain at home, and over at the community center, too. My husband gets so frustrated because he says he can't count on me to keep our plans straight. And the other volunteers at the center are starting to feel the same way. They feel like someone always has to check behind me to make sure I've actually done what I said I'd do. \n\nLike last week, I was supposed to organize the canned goods for the food drive. We do a big food drive every Thanksgiving, and people are so generous, they really are. But you wouldn't believe how many people donate expired cans! I found a can of cranberry sauce from 2018! Who keeps cranberry sauce for five years? And it was the jellied kind, too. I always prefer the whole berry kind myself, it just tastes more authentic, don't you think? My mother used to make it from scratch, boiling the berries on the stove until they popped. The whole house would smell so wonderful and tart. \n\nAnyway, I was supposed to be sorting the cans by expiration date, but I got to chatting with Mrs. Higgins—she just had her hip replaced, you know, and she was telling me all about the physical therapy, which sounds just dreadful—and I ended up putting the vegetables with the soups, and I completely forgot to check the dates on half the boxes. The center director had to come in and redo the whole thing. So... yes, I guess you could say my scattering about does interfere with things quite a bit.",
